# Pinned tool versions for the bare-metal probe box.
#
# CONSUMED BY EXACTLY ONE FILE: infra/provision/common-system.sh.
#
# It is NOT read by infra/lima/overdrive-dev.yaml — Lima keeps its own `param:`
# block, hand-maintained, and the two are kept aligned by eye. Saying otherwise
# here would be a claim the code does not support.
#
# Shell-sourceable: `set -a; . infra/provision/versions.env; set +a`

# Cloud Hypervisor. v46.0 is what the spike validated end to end — it boots the
# guest, and it carries `--landlock` / `--landlock-rules`, which P5 depends on.
#
# NOTE: do NOT adopt the "CH >= 48.0" floor from the opencapsule reference
# implementation. That number appears in six of its documents with no stated
# reason, its startup check was never built, and v46.0 demonstrably has the
# capability we actually need. Name a floor against a capability or not at all.
CLOUD_HYPERVISOR_VERSION="v46.0"

# virtiofsd comes from apt (Ubuntu ships 1.13.2), NOT a pinned download.
# It lands at /usr/libexec/virtiofsd and is NOT on $PATH — `which virtiofsd`
# returns nothing. Anything invoking it must use the absolute path.
VIRTIOFSD_BIN="/usr/libexec/virtiofsd"

# NOTE: wasmtime and pwru are deliberately absent. Lima installs both; this box
# does not, because nothing in the microVM probes uses them. They were listed
# here briefly as dead variables, which implied the metal box got them. It does
# not — add them to common-system.sh first if that changes.
